WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.828
This briefing is Book 10 of the
Federal Modernization Workbook,

3
00:00:04.828 --> 00:00:06.900
Cloud Boundary and Landing Zone.

4
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.668
Its argument is simple: the authorization
boundary, not the product catalog,

5
00:00:11.668 --> 00:00:15.225
decides which cloud features
an agency can actually use.

6
00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:17.037
We'll take four questions in turn.

7
00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:19.576
Why does the boundary
decide what you can use?

8
00:00:19.576 --> 00:00:20.825
What has to change?

9
00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:22.225
Who owns the boundary?

10
00:00:22.225 --> 00:00:23.413
And how do you get there?

11
00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:28.347
If you remember one thing, make it this:
treat the boundary as a list you can read,

12
00:00:28.347 --> 00:00:33.513
not a perimeter you can only accept, and
evidence every choice in your own package.

13
00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:38.675
The slides and notes carry every detail
and citation; I'll stick to what matters.

14
00:00:38.675 --> 00:00:41.090
Let's start with why the boundary decides.
